From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:59:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Linux host: ArbitrateLock, ArbitrateUnlock,
 WaitProcessWideKeyAtomic and SignalProcessWideKey can run in C (#19)

With NX2LINUX_SVC_NATIVE=1 and libnx2linux_sync.so built, the four calls on
mutex words and keys are answered by the library, behind the svc hook of the
previous patch. They are one group because they share the waiter queues.
The library keeps what Horizon.svc keeps: the count of each call, the last
call of each thread (thread_report reads it) and its last 16. A run that
asks for NX2LINUX_SVC_PROFILE, NX2LINUX_SVC_RING or --verbose stays in
Python and says so. Off by default. Tests: both implementations run the
same scenarios and must give the same answers and words, then both are
run under contention, and the calls run through the real AOT runtime.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The four mutex and condition-key kernel calls run in C behind NX2LINUX_SVC_NATIVE, off by default, to take them out of the GIL
Issue: Sunshine-Off/NX2Linux#19

